  "prefLabel": "Sep 403.05 Exemptions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Sep 403.05 Exemptions.\n\n(a) A licensee may request a waiver from the continuing education requirements, pursuant to Sep 201.02(j), for any of the following reasons:\n\n(1) A licensee serving on temporary active duty in the armed forces of the United States for a period of time exceeding 120 consecutive days in a year shall be exempt from obtaining the continuing education hours required during that year; or\n\n(2) Licensees experiencing disability, illness, or other extenuating circumstances which would prevent the licensee from completing the required continuing education hours.\n\n(b) A licensee seeking a waiver shall file the request as required by Plc 211.03 through Plc 211.05.\n\nSource. #12654, eff 10-31-18; ss by #14361, eff 10-26-25, EXPIRES: 10-26-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/sep100-700.html"
